# punused findings adjudicated as false positives. One literal substring per
# line, matched against punused's output line; full-line `#` comments carry the
# reason. Invalid-by-construction classes: `.kiro/steering/tools.md`.
#
# transportError is constructed in non-test code in internal/notify/discord.go --
# by safeTransportError on every client.Do failure -- and flows out as `error`
# through post -> httpx.Do -> watch. So every use is interface dispatch or a
# stdlib errors.* traversal, which punused cannot see (bep/punused#3).
#
# Error() satisfies the builtin error interface; the text surfaces through
# httpx.Do's per-attempt logging and watch's failure lines.
method (transportError).Error
#
# transportError.Unwrap is decision-changing, not decorative: watch's
# sendMissing/sendHistory/sendRecovered test errors.Is(err, context.Canceled),
# and Error() renders only the phrase, so the cause is reachable ONLY through
# Unwrap. Without it a shutdown-abandoned send is misread as a delivery failure,
# moving the notification counters and logging an error on every shutdown.
# httpx's retry classifier also reads the chain for net.Error / ECONNRESET /
# ECONNREFUSED / DNSError, so dropping Unwrap would silently disable per-attempt
# retry of transport failures.
method (transportError).Unwrap
